.policy "ruff-pyi030-unnecessary-literal-union" revision 2
.description "Merge the Literal members of a union into a single Literal listing all the values; it means the same thing and is shorter."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI030 (flake8-pyi), every file: a union with two or more `Literal[…]` members, which can be one
// Literal. Nested unions are flattened and reported once, at the outermost; `|` counts anywhere, at runtime too.
//   x: Literal[1] | Literal[2] | None      ← PYI030: write `Literal[1, 2] | None`
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI030(at: node) code "PYI030" "Merge the `Literal[...]` members of this union into one `Literal[...]`, keeping the other members, e.g. `Literal[1, 2] | str`; leave it alone if fewer than two members are `Literal[...]`."
    suppress ruff "PYI030"
PYI030(u) :- union_top(u), count : { union_leaf(u, m), typing_subscript(m, "Literal") } >= 2.
